      "message": "[Gerrit AI Review] Since `start_new_session\u003dTrue` is used in `subprocess.Popen`, the spawned process is the leader of its new process group, meaning its PID is exactly its PGID.\n\nYou can simplify `os.getpgid(self.process.pid)` to just `self.process.pid`. This is also slightly more robust because `os.getpgid()` could theoretically raise a `ProcessLookupError` if the group leader has already terminated and been reaped, which would bypass the `os.killpg()` call entirely and potentially leave child processes orphaned.\n\n```python\n                os.killpg(self.process.pid, signal.SIGKILL)\n```",
